; ============================================================
;  RIG REBALANCE - NO RED SQUARES
;
;  OVERRIDES Squared Away's numbers with ! rather than shipping its
;  64 KB system file again.
;
;  THE CHANGE THAT MATTERS: a rig has no medical pocket at all. Not
;  one, at any tier. A red square - the only place a MEDKIT is quick -
;  comes from a pouch you bought and from nowhere else.
;
;  WHY. Two reasons, and the second is the honest one.
;
;  The fiction: a chest rig is webbing and pockets. A medical pouch is
;  a thing you ADD because you decided to carry medicine. Medkit speed
;  should be a purchase, never a gift.
;
;  The economy: a rig recipe that names its own slots has to buy them,
;  and a red square is priced as a scarce prize. Prizes make terrible
;  ingredients - at the old prices, crafting a rig cost three to five
;  times buying one. Taking red out of the rig takes it out of the
;  recipe, and the problem disappears rather than being managed.
;
;  YOU ARE NOT LEFT WITHOUT FAST MEDICINE. A green square is quick for
;  BANDAGES, and every rig has three to six of them. Only medkits and
;  the rest of the pharmacy need red, and that is what the medic's
;  pouches are for.
;
;  THE REST OF THE RULES
;    2x2 is tier 5 only, two rigs have one
;    3x1 is tier 2 and up
;    magazine pockets are FEW: one at tier 1, two at tier 3, three at
;      tier 4 and 5. A rig is not a magazine rack.
;    green climbs 3 to 6 - supplies are what a rig gains as it grows
;    two pouch slots on every rig, whatever its tier
;
;  TIER 5, one choice rather than three steps:
;    Tarzan   two drums and a magazine
;    Shturm   a drum, a deep row and a magazine - both, less of each
;    Rubezh   two deep rows and a magazine, and the cheapest of the
;             three. No drum at all, and it carries the most.
;
;  Yellow pockets are written TALL x WIDE, like the mod: a 2x1 is a
;  magazine standing up. Green are single squares.
; ============================================================

